dif@bhprtc.scpd.oz.au (David Faulkner) writes:

>In a game yesterday I picked up 7 candles. I lit them to explore some of
>the mines, expecting that they would burn one at a time, and after one
>went out I would be left with six. But not so, the candle went out and I
>found all seven had burnt. And they burnt only as long as one candle,
>and lit the same area.


In wizard mode I discovered that they are only all lit when they are in
the same inventory slot -- cursed candles are not lit when uncursed candles
are, and candles in a bag remain unlit.  It looks like the notion of lit/
unlit should be separated from inventory slot, because otherwise the
player is penalized by the grouping of the pack order mechanism, and
needs a pack, or needs to curse some of his candles, etc., which is
artificial.

-jim


